Had jei meant "whether" it would have been VERY useful. If
usage of jei has been limited it is because (a) its true
"truthvalue" meaning is pretty useless, and (b) most users
realized that using "jei" to mean "whether" would be erroneous
(even though I am sure that "jei" was created with the intention
that it mean "whether", but then given an incorrect but
subsequently binding definition).

